From 52ea98725b9715200f90cac9ac5b3e514912b352 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FNGarvin <184324400+FNGarvin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:25:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] Rework media dump to hook MediaFormatReader instead of
 MSE only

Move the capture point from SourceBuffer::AppendData (MSE-only) down to
MediaFormatReader::OnVideoDemuxCompleted/OnAudioDemuxCompleted, the point
where every playback pipeline -- MSE, blob-backed, or a plain URL -- has
already converged before decode. This makes "Dump Media Stream" work
regardless of how a page is feeding the <video>/<audio> element, not just
MSE-backed ones.

Demuxed samples are muxed into a single combined Matroska (.mkv) file via
the new MediaDumpMuxer, which reuses Gecko's existing low-level EBML
primitives (the same ones WebMWriter uses for MediaRecorder) but, unlike
that writer, reads each track's actual codec ID and codec-private config
from its TrackInfo instead of hardcoding VP8+Opus. Currently wired up for
VP8/VP9 video and Opus/Vorbis audio; H.264+AAC needs further codec-private
reformatting work and isn't included yet.

Encrypted (EME/DRM) samples are dropped at the sample level rather than
relying on never attaching to begin with.

Removes the superseded SourceBuffer-specific MseStreamDumper mechanism.
